yaml/number/decimal
description: Integer or float in base ten
- >
  A decimal integer or float — a SUPERCLASS of
  [json/number](::language:01-Concretes_2:04-json_code:01-json_scalar:01-json_number): every
  JSON number reads as a YAML decimal, and YAML also allows a bare leading or trailing point
  and an explicit plus:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  a: 42
  b: -0.5
  c: 3.14e2
  d: .5
  e: +1
- *..:..:..:..:..:04-json_code:01-json_scalar:01-json_number
